    description: "WHAT. Fold the old spellings of \"how a call's target was chosen\" into the resolution mark, one language at a time,\nin the commit that moves that language's analyzer onto the shared call-resolution pass. Owner's rule for the\nrollout (shared_resolution_design_11242026.md): each language's commit deletes what the shared pass replaced.\n\nTHE FOLDS (audit docs/audits/0030, per-value table).\n- evidence_type ast_call_type_inferred, ast_method_type_inferred, ast_call_extension, ast_call_ufcs,\n  ast_call_inherited_method, ast_call_inherited_field -> ast_call + mark receiver_type\n- evidence_type ast_method_this, ast_call_this, ast_method_this_property, ast_call_this_property,\n  ast_call_inherited -> ast_call + mark own_type\n- evidence_type ast_call_static, ast_static_call, ast_call_namespace -> ast_call + mark qualified\n- evidence_type ast_method_inferred -> ast_call + mark name\n- resolution_quality typed, typed_receiver, type_inferred, chained_return_type (resolved edges) -> mark receiver_type\n- resolution_quality recovery -> mark class_hint; resolution_quality ambiguous (resolved edges) -> mark name\n- receiver typed_var, typed_field, declared_type -> mark receiver_type; self -> own_type; qualified -> qualified\n- disambiguation_fallback -> mark name (INV-zuhub's confidence rule then keys on the mark)\nNOT FOLDED: receiver bare / generic / field_chain (expression shape); resolution_quality accessor_name (ADR-0053);\nevery value on unresolved edges.\n\nNEEDS AN OWNER RULING FIRST. The evidence_type folds move confidence bands (ADR-0039: each value has a registered\nbase), and audit 0004 holds those values CANONICAL on the evidence-type axis. The ADR that follows audit 0030 must\nsupersede both by number.\n\nGUARD ALREADY IN PLACE (built with the mark): a test pins the number of emit sites of each old spelling per source\nfile; the number may only go down.\n\nDONE WHEN no source file under packages/*/src emits a folded value and the pinned table is empty."  # af8e
    fields: {}  # af8e
